<%# locals: (active:, title: nil, badge: nil, tabs: [], tab_active: nil, title_action: nil, right_content: nil) %>
<%# The head of a page of the management area. Since 2026-11-11 the sections are
    the sidebar's list while the area is open (common/_navigation_management,
    doc/verwaltung_seitennavigation_plan.md), so this head is the page head of
    every other page: the title names the SECTION (`active`, a key of
    NavigationHelper::SETTINGS_TABS), the organisation below, the tools right of
    it (right_content; the main action as title_action, outermost, #143).

    tabs: the section's own pages, where it has some (the members and their access
    overview); tab_active names the open one. The title stays the section's on every
    tab (user, 2026-11-11). Without tabs there is no bar.

    Title box and bar come from organisations/shared/_subnav, which the times area
    renders as well: one owner of the left edge and the active marker. Access is
    checked per page via Pundit. %>
<%= render 'organisations/shared/subnav',
      tabs: tabs,
      active: tab_active || active,
      aria_label: title || management_section_label(active),
      title: title || management_section_label(active),
      badge: badge,
      title_action: title_action,
      right_content: right_content %>
